{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"SB0300","billNumberShort":"S.B. 300","billNumberLong":"SB0300","fileNumber":"2026FL1305","shortTitle":"Single Payer Health Insurance Amendments","currentSubVersion":"0","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"BLOUIN","primeSponsorName":"Sen. Blouin, Nate","primeSponsorHouse":"S","floorSponsor":"","floorSponsorName":"","floorSponsorHouse":"","generalProvisions":"This bill establishes a state operated health financing program.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>establishes a state operated health financing program;<hr><ltbullet>creates the Utah Health Services Commission;<hr><ltbullet>establishes duties for the Utah Health Services Commission;<hr><ltbullet>moves health workforce councils and offices from the Department of Health and Human Services to the Utah Health Services Commission;<hr><ltbullet>directs the Department of Health and Human Services to begin transitioning the operation and management of the Medicaid program to the state operated health financing program;<hr><ltbullet>transitions the Public Employees' Benefit and Insurance Program into a state operated health financing program that is open to the public;<hr><ltbullet>allows all state residents to enroll in the state operated health financing program;<hr><ltbullet>prohibits billing by health care facilities;<hr><ltbullet>requires the state operated health financing program to begin billing on behalf of health care facilities;<hr><ltbullet>requires all government entities to transition government employees to the state operated health financing program;<hr><ltbullet>repeals certain unnecessary or obsolete programs; and<hr><ltbullet>creates a tax to fund the state operated health financing program.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Christopher Williams","fiscalAnalyst":"Sean C. Faherty","lastAction":"Senate/ filed","lastActionOwner":"Senate file for bills not passed","lastActionDate":"3/6/2026","trackingID"